{
  "result": "If I had one wish to change the world, I would make true empathy effortless.\n\nNot just being nice to each other - but actually being able to *feel* and *understand* what someone else is going through for a moment. To instantly understand why someone is scared, why they believe what they believe, what they're carrying that you can't see.\n\nI think so many of the world's biggest problems - conflict, loneliness, hate, inequality - come from that gap in understanding. We judge what we don't understand, and we fear what we judge.\n\nIf everyone could truly feel each other's perspective, even for a few minutes a day, I think kindness would become automatic. People would still disagree, but they'd do it with respect. They'd still have different lives and beliefs, but they'd have compassion underneath it all.\n\nWe'd take better care of each other and the planet because we'd feel connected to it, not separate from it.\n\nWhat about you? If you could change one thing, what would it be?",
